    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93448" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σαυνῖται</span></b> , οἱ,
			<u>Samnites</u>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>GDI</u>
			2000.4
		</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			5.4.11
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			12
		</span></i> (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σανν-</span>
			): so <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σαυνῖτις</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, ἡ,
				<u>Samnium</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.90.7
			</span></i>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σαυνίτιδες [πόλεις</span>]
				<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				5.4.11
			</span></i>. (Osc. <u>Safinim</u> (from
			*<i>Sa[bstrok]niom</i>); <i><span class="en">
				Fest.
				p.437
			</span></i> L. wrongly derives Lat. <u>Samnites</u> from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαύνιον</span>.)</div>
